---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title       = `Molly / MDMA Safety Guide: Test Kits, Supplements & Real Evidence | Rave Wellness`;
const description = `Evidence-based molly guide: test for fentanyl, use magnesium for jaw clenching, time your 5-HTP correctly, and see what the research actually says about how often is really safe. Cited science throughout.`;
const keywords    = `MDMA harm reduction, MDMA supplement protocol, how to test MDMA for fentanyl, MDMA 3 month rule, molly harm reduction, ecstasy safety guide, rave pills harm reduction, ecstasy pills testing, MDMA NAC supplement, rolling safely MDMA, MDMA dosing, MDMA fentanyl test strips, MDMA serotonin syndrome, MDMA drug interactions, reagent test MDMA, MDMA magnesium jaw clenching bruxism, MDMA magnesium jaw clenching evidence, magnesium bruxism MDMA harm reduction, green tea extract MDMA, green tea extract EGCG MDMA 5-HTP, 5-HTP MDMA, 5-HTP molly, 5 htp and molly, vitamin C MDMA, vitamin C molly, what is molly drug, MDMA test kit, dancesafe MDMA supplements magnesium NAC 5-HTP antioxidants, MDMA street names, Molly drug, Ecstasy drug, E drug, X drug, XTC drug, Mandy drug, pills rave, beans drug, rolls drug, MDM drug`;
const canonical   = `https://www.ravewellness.org/mdma.html`;
const ogTitle     = `Molly / MDMA Safety Guide: Test Kits, Supplements & Real Evidence | Rave Wellness`;
const ogDesc      = `Fentanyl testing, NAC + magnesium + 5-HTP supplement protocol, safe dosing, dangerous combinations, and what peer-reviewed research says about MDMA frequency. Free guide.`;
const twTitle     = ``;
const twDesc      = ``;
const schemaJson  = `{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://www.ravewellness.org/mdma.html#article",
        "headline": "MDMA Harm Reduction: The Complete Guide to Testing, Supplements, and Safe Use",
        "description": "Complete MDMA harm reduction guide covering reagent testing, fentanyl detection, timed supplement protocol, temperature management, dangerous drug combinations, and evidence-based use frequency guidance.",
        "url": "https://www.ravewellness.org/mdma.html",
        "mainEntityOfPage": "https://www.ravewellness.org/mdma.html",
        "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Rave Wellness", "url": "https://www.ravewellness.org" },
        "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Rave Wellness", "url": "https://www.ravewellness.org" },
        "about": [
          { "@type": "Thing", "name": "MDMA" },
          { "@type": "Thing", "name": "Harm reduction" },
          { "@type": "Thing", "name": "Drug testing" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "itemListElement": [
          { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.ravewellness.org/" },
          { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "MDMA Harm Reduction", "item": "https://www.ravewellness.org/mdma.html" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How do I test MDMA for fentanyl?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Dissolve a small amount (~10mg) of MDMA in water (about ¼ tsp). Dip a fentanyl test strip for 15 seconds, lay flat, and read after 2–5 minutes. One line means fentanyl detected, do not use. Two lines means negative at that sensitivity threshold. Always combine with reagent testing (Marquis, Mecke, Simon's) for full confirmation."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What supplements should I take with MDMA?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "The evidence-based MDMA supplement protocol: 48 hours before, NAC 600mg twice daily, Vitamin C 1000mg, Alpha Lipoic Acid 100mg. 60 minutes before, NAC 1200mg, ALCAR 500mg, Magnesium Glycinate 400mg, Vitamin C 1000mg, CoQ10 200mg. During, electrolytes and optional Magnesium 200mg. 24 hours after, 5-HTP 100mg + EGCG 400mg three times daily, NAC 600mg, Vitamin C, Melatonin. Never take 5-HTP during or within 24 hours of MDMA."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is a safe dose of MDMA?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "MDMA doses: light (50–75mg), common (75–125mg), high (125–175mg). Always start low with any new batch. Neurotoxicity scales with dose, higher doses produce more serotonin release and oxidative byproducts. Without a milligram scale you cannot know your actual dose from crystals or powder. If redosing, take once at half the original dose maximum."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the 3-month rule for MDMA, and is it based on science?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "The '3-month rule' originated from Ann Shulgin's personal clinical observation, not a controlled study. Spacing matters, but the biology involves three distinct processes: (1) 5-HT2A receptor desensitization (days to weeks, the primary driver of 'losing the magic' in occasional users); (2) depletion of the releasable serotonin pool (weeks); and (3) structural SERT reduction from axon terminal damage (months to years, documented only in heavy users). Human neuroimaging studies showing 6–18+ month recovery timelines enrolled subjects with a median of 50–244 lifetime uses (Erritzoe 2011; Selvaraj 2009), occasional users fall entirely outside those study populations. MAPS Phase 3 trials used ~4-week intervals but in a limited 3-session clinical context. For occasional users, 'losing the magic' is primarily receptor desensitization, not structural damage. The real risk drivers are total lifetime uses, dose per session, hot environments, and binge re-dosing. Longer gaps are better; 3 months is a reasonable conservative heuristic, not a scientifically derived threshold."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What drugs are dangerous to combine with MDMA?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "The most dangerous MDMA combinations: MAOIs (potentially fatal serotonin syndrome), SSRIs/SNRIs (serotonin syndrome risk; also unpredictably blunts effects), Lithium (seizure risk), Tramadol (serotonin syndrome), DXM/cough syrup (serotonin syndrome), stimulants like cocaine or amphetamines (severe cardiovascular strain). Check all medications, prescription, OTC, and recreational, before combining."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How do I manage temperature while using MDMA?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Temperature management is the highest-leverage MDMA harm reduction intervention. Research shows maintaining normal body temperature can nearly eliminate serotonergic neurotoxicity even at high doses. Take 10–15 minute breaks from dancing every hour, seek air conditioning or cool outdoor air, use wet cloths on the neck and wrists, and avoid heavy layers. Know where the cool areas are in the venue before you need them."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Does magnesium reduce jaw clenching (bruxism) on MDMA?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Yes. Magnesium glycinate is widely used in harm reduction to reduce MDMA-induced jaw clenching (bruxism). MDMA floods dopaminergic pathways in the basal ganglia, triggering involuntary jaw muscle contractions. Magnesium acts as a natural NMDA receptor antagonist and calcium channel modulator, dampening the excitatory signaling that drives these contractions. Magnesium deficiency is also independently associated with elevated bruxism rates. The glycinate form has superior bioavailability and is gentler on the stomach. Standard protocol: 400mg taken 60 minutes before, with an optional 200mg redose if clenching is severe. This recommendation is part of the DanceSafe harm reduction supplement protocol."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Why take green tea extract (EGCG) with 5-HTP after MDMA?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "EGCG (epigallocatechin gallate, the active compound in green tea extract) is taken alongside 5-HTP to prevent peripheral conversion of 5-HTP to serotonin before it reaches the brain. Without EGCG, the enzyme aromatic L-amino acid decarboxylase (AADC) converts much of the 5-HTP to serotonin in the gut and blood vessels, where it cannot cross the blood-brain barrier and may cause nausea, GI distress, or cardiovascular effects. EGCG inhibits peripheral AADC activity, directing more 5-HTP toward brain serotonin synthesis where replenishment is needed. Always take EGCG (400mg) together with each dose of 5-HTP. Never take 5-HTP or EGCG during or within 24 hours of MDMA use, serotonin syndrome risk."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }`;
---

<BaseLayout
  {title}
  {description}
  {keywords}
  {canonical}
  ogTitle={ogTitle}
  ogDescription={ogDesc}
  twitterTitle={twTitle}
  twitterDescription={twDesc}
  {schemaJson}
>
  <Fragment slot="footer-orgs">
    <a href="https://dancesafe.org/r/ravewellness/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DanceSafe</a>
            <a href="https://maps.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MAPS</a>
            <a href="https://tripsit.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TripSit</a>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="footer-nav">
    <h4>On This Page</h4>
              <a href="#test">Test Your Substance</a>
              <a href="#protocol">Supplement Protocol</a>
              <a href="#during">During Use</a>
              <a href="#recovery">Recovery</a>
              <a href="#research">Research</a>
              <a href="#shop">Shop</a>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="footer-emergency">
    <h4>Emergency Resources</h4>
              <p><strong>If someone is in distress:</strong></p>
              <ul>
                <li>Call emergency services (911 in US)</li>
                <li>SAMHSA Helpline: 1-800-662-4357</li>
                <li>Poison Control: 1-800-222-1222</li>
              </ul>
  </Fragment>

<main>

    <!-- ===== HERO ===== -->
    <section id="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <div class="hero-badge">MDMA Harm Reduction Guide</div>
          <h1>MDMA Harm Reduction:<br /><span>Test, Prepare & Roll Safer.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">Evidence-based protocols, supplement guides, and peer-reviewed research to reduce the risks of MDMA use. Street names: Molly, Ecstasy, E, X, XTC, Mandy, Pills, Beans, Rolls. Because information saves lives.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a href="#test" class="btn btn-primary">Start: Test Your Substance</a>
            <a href="#protocol" class="btn btn-ghost">View Supplement Protocol</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-disclaimer">
          <span class="disclaimer-icon">⚠</span>
          <p><strong>This is not medical advice.</strong> MDMA is illegal in most countries and carries real risks. This information is for people who have already decided to use and want to minimize harm. If you're experiencing a medical emergency, call emergency services immediately. Some links on this page are affiliate links, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== RISK OVERVIEW ===== -->
    <section id="risks">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-title centered">The Four Critical Risks</h2>
        <div class="risk-grid">
          <div class="risk-card risk-critical">
            <div class="risk-icon">☠</div>
            <h3>Contaminated Supply</h3>
            <p>Studies show the majority of pills sold as MDMA contain adulterants. Fentanyl is increasingly detected in stimulants. Test every time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-card risk-high">
            <div class="risk-icon">🧠</div>
            <h3>Serotonin Neurotoxicity</h3>
            <p>High doses and frequent use are associated with long-term reductions in serotonin transporter density. Antioxidants and spacing use may reduce this.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-card risk-critical">
            <div class="risk-icon">🌡</div>
            <h3>Hyperthermia</h3>
            <p>Overheating dramatically amplifies neurotoxicity and is a primary cause of MDMA-related deaths. Temperature management is non-negotiable.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="risk-card risk-critical">
            <div class="risk-icon">💊</div>
            <h3>Dangerous Drug Interactions</h3>
            <p>Combining MDMA with SSRIs, MAOIs, or lithium can cause fatal serotonin syndrome. Check every medication you take.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== STEP 1: TEST ===== -->
    <section id="test">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="step-pill">Step 1</div>
          <h2>Always Test Your Substance</h2>
          <p class="section-sub">The single most important harm reduction action. Test before every use, even if you've used the same batch before. Fentanyl contamination is real and increasing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="test-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-icon-wrap icon-purple">🧪</div>
            <h3>Reagent Testing</h3>
            <p>Chemical reagents react with specific substances to produce color changes. Use all three for MDMA confirmation:</p>
            <div class="reagent-table">
              <div class="reagent-row header">
                <span>Reagent</span>
                <span>MDMA Result</span>
              </div>
              <div class="reagent-row">
                <span class="reagent-name">Marquis</span>
                <span class="result result-purple">Purple → Black</span>
              </div>
              <div class="reagent-row">
                <span class="reagent-name">Mecke</span>
                <span class="result result-blue">Blue → Black</span>
              </div>
              <div class="reagent-row">
                <span class="reagent-name">Simon's</span>
                <span class="result result-blue">Blue (confirms MDMA vs. MDA)</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="note-text">Using all three together gives the highest confidence. No test is 100%, they indicate presence, not purity or dose.</p>
            <a href="https://dancesafe.org/product/mdma-testing-kit/r/ravewellness/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary">Get MDMA Test Kit at DanceSafe →</a>
          </div>

          <div class="card card-danger">
            <div class="card-icon-wrap icon-red">🚨</div>
            <h3>Fentanyl Test Strips</h3>
            <p class="danger-text"><strong>A dose as small as 2mg of fentanyl can be fatal.</strong> Test every batch, every time. No exceptions.</p>
            <div class="instruction-box">
              <h4>How to Test MDMA for Fentanyl:</h4>
              <ol>
                <li>Dissolve a small amount (~10mg) in water (about ¼ tsp)</li>
                <li>Dip the strip for 15 seconds</li>
                <li>Lay flat and read results after 2–5 minutes</li>
                <li class="result-critical"><strong>1 line = fentanyl detected. Do not use.</strong></li>
                <li>2 lines = negative (fentanyl not detected at that sensitivity)</li>
              </ol>
            </div>
            <p class="note-text">Strips don't detect all analogs. A negative result does not guarantee safety. Also use <strong>xylazine ("tranq") test strips</strong> on the same liquid sample, xylazine is appearing in non-opioid powders and is not reversed by naloxone alone.</p>
            <div class="btn-row">
              <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0B1N7Z1CH?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-sm btn-danger">Get Fentanyl Strips →</a>
              <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=xylazine+test+strip+BNTX&tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-sm btn-secondary">Xylazine test strips (BTNX) →</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-icon-wrap icon-teal">🔬</div>
            <h3>Drug Checking Services</h3>
            <p>Advanced testing (FTIR, GCMS) can quantify purity and identify unknown substances. More accurate than reagents alone.</p>
            <ul class="resource-list">
              <li>
                <a href="https://dancesafe.org/r/ravewellness/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DanceSafe</a>
                <span>,  Operates at events; distributes test kits</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="https://tripsit.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TripSit</a>
                <span>,  Drug info and combination checker</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span>Local harm reduction organizations</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="note-text">Some cities offer free community drug checking programs. Search for local services in your area.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== STEP 2: SUPPLEMENT PROTOCOL ===== -->
    <section id="protocol">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="step-pill">Step 2</div>
          <h2>The Supplement Protocol</h2>
          <p class="section-sub">MDMA's neurotoxic potential is primarily mediated by oxidative stress. These supplements may reduce that damage, evidence is primarily from animal studies. Core protocol supplements: <strong>NAC</strong> (glutathione precursor), <strong>Magnesium</strong> (jaw clenching / bruxism), <strong>5-HTP + EGCG</strong> (serotonin recovery). This protocol reflects recommendations from <a href="https://dancesafe.org/r/ravewellness/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DanceSafe</a> and the broader harm reduction community. No protocol eliminates risk, and no supplement replaces testing or appropriate dosing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="protocol-timeline">

          <!-- T-48h -->
          <div class="timeline-card">
            <div class="timeline-label">T − 48 hours</div>
            <h3>Pre-Loading</h3>
            <p class="timeline-desc">Build antioxidant reserves in the days before.</p>
            <div class="supp-list">
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">NAC</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">600mg × 2 daily</span>
                </div>
                <p>N-Acetyl Cysteine, direct precursor to glutathione, the brain's primary endogenous antioxidant. Supplies the cysteine needed for glutathione synthesis. Builds reserves before MDMA exposure.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013OUQ3S?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy NAC →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Glycine</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">1000mg daily</span>
                </div>
                <p>The second rate-limiting precursor for glutathione, alongside cysteine (from NAC). Research by Sekhar et al. (Baylor) shows that the GlyNAC combination restores glutathione significantly more effectively than NAC alone, because both precursors must be present for glutathione synthase to function at full capacity. Take together with NAC.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013OVZJW?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy Glycine →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Vitamin C</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">1000mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Water-soluble antioxidant with demonstrated neuroprotective effects in oxidative stress models.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013OSLKI?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy Vitamin C →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Alpha Lipoic Acid</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">100mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Universal antioxidant, functions in both water and fat-soluble environments, and helps regenerate Vitamins C and E.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B005C99OWO?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy ALA (R-form) →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- T-60min -->
          <div class="timeline-card timeline-primary">
            <div class="timeline-label">T − 60 minutes</div>
            <h3>Pre-Dosing</h3>
            <p class="timeline-desc">Load up right before, the most critical window.</p>
            <div class="supp-list">
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">NAC</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">1200mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Higher pre-dose to maximize glutathione availability during peak MDMA metabolism.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013OUQ3S?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy NAC →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">ALCAR</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">500mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Acetyl-L-Carnitine, crosses the blood-brain barrier and supports mitochondrial energy production under metabolic stress.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0027DWNHQ?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy ALCAR →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Magnesium Glycinate</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">400mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Reduces jaw clenching (bruxism), one of the most common and uncomfortable effects of MDMA. <strong>How it works:</strong> MDMA floods dopaminergic pathways in the basal ganglia, triggering involuntary jaw muscle contractions. Magnesium acts as a natural NMDA receptor antagonist and voltage-gated calcium channel modulator, dampening the excitatory signaling driving these contractions. Magnesium deficiency is also independently associated with elevated bruxism rates in the general population. Glycinate form has superior bioavailability and is gentler on the stomach than oxide or citrate.</p>
                <p class="note-text">This is one of the best-documented experiential benefits of the harm reduction supplement protocol, <a href="https://dancesafe.org/r/ravewellness/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DanceSafe</a> and other harm reduction organizations consistently recommend it.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B000BD0RT0?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy Magnesium →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Vitamin C</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">1000mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Antioxidant loading before MDMA begins metabolizing. Use buffered form to reduce stomach upset.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013OSLKI?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy Vitamin C →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">CoQ10</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">200mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Coenzyme Q10, essential component of the mitochondrial electron transport chain; supports cellular energy production and acts as a fat-soluble antioxidant.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B015TK6KVI?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy CoQ10 →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- During -->
          <div class="timeline-card timeline-during">
            <div class="timeline-label">During</div>
            <h3>Active Use</h3>
            <p class="timeline-desc">Minimal supplements, focus on safety basics.</p>
            <div class="supp-list">
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Magnesium</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">200mg if needed</span>
                </div>
                <p>Optional redose if jaw clenching is severe.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Electrolytes</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">Per packet / as needed</span>
                </div>
                <p>Add to water when sweating. Critical for preventing hyponatremia. See hydration guide below.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07TT8B1JJ?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy LMNT →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="during-warning">
              <strong>⚠ NEVER take 5-HTP during or within 24 hours of MDMA.</strong> Combining serotonin precursors with MDMA risks serotonin syndrome, a potentially fatal condition.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="recovery-split">
          <div class="timeline-card timeline-recovery">
            <div class="timeline-label">Same night, home</div>
            <h3>Right when you get back</h3>
            <p class="timeline-desc">Rehydrate and set up sleep, <strong>do not start 5-HTP the same night</strong> as rolling. Serotonin precursors combined with MDMA still in your system can contribute to serotonin syndrome.</p>
            <div class="supp-list">
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Water + electrolytes</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">Sip steadily</span>
                </div>
                <p>Replace fluids and salts you sweated out. Electrolytes beat plain water alone for preventing headache and malaise the next day.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07TT8B1JJ?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Electrolyte packets →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">NAC</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">600mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Continue antioxidant support, glutathione production is still needed while MDMA metabolites clear your system.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013OUQ3S?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy NAC →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Vitamin C</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">1000mg</span>
                </div>
                <p>Antioxidant support while you sleep, take with water.</p>
                <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013OSLKI?tag=ravewellness01-20" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="supp-link">Buy Vitamin C →</a>
              </div>
              <div class="supp-item supp-featured">
                <div class="supp-header">
                  <span class="supp-name">Melatonin</span>
                  <span class="supp-dose">3–5mg before bed</span>
                </div>
