        <div class="protocol-caveat">
          <h4>Evidence Caveat</h4>
          <p>The antioxidant mechanism is well-supported: MDMA neurotoxicity is substantially mediated by oxidative stress and reactive oxygen species produced during serotonin metabolism and MDMA's dopamine-in-serotonin-terminal effect. Specific animal studies show protective effects, alpha-lipoic acid fully prevented serotonin depletion in rats (Aguirre et al., 1999); ALCAR preserved mitochondrial integrity (PubMed 19015003); Vitamin C suppressed hydroxyl radical generation and prevented 5-HT loss (Shankaran &amp; Gudelsky, 2001); NAC protected hippocampal structure and improved memory outcomes (PubMed 25096201). Pre-treatment timing is most studied; post-use supplementation within 24 hours may also help given that oxidative stress peaks as MDMA is metabolized. However, all protective studies used injected doses in rodents, oral bioavailability at human doses is lower, and <strong>no controlled human trials exist</strong>. These supplements have genuine mechanistic support but unproven human efficacy. They are generally safe when used as directed. Consult a healthcare provider about interactions with any medications.</p>
